@startuml
title GoalZone - Automated triggers and external payment boundary
left to right direction
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam actorStyle awesome
skinparam usecase {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #0369A1
  ArrowColor #475569
}

actor "Booking event" as Event
actor "Scheduled time" as Time
actor "PayPal Sandbox" as PayPal

rectangle GoalZone {
  package "Synchronous business rules" #ECFDF5 {
    usecase "UC-18\nValidate add-on availability" as UC18
    usecase "UC-28\nConfirm eligible booking" as UC28
    usecase "UC-40\nCapture/confirm online payment" as UC40
    usecase "UC-44\nGenerate/update invoice" as UC44
    usecase "UC-52\nValidate/apply promotion" as UC52
    usecase "UC-63\nRank live slot suggestions" as UC63
  }
  package "Scheduled & event notifications" #EFF6FF {
    usecase "UC-42\nExpire unpaid hold" as UC42
    usecase "UC-56\nSend booking confirmation" as UC56
    usecase "UC-57\nSend booking reminder" as UC57
    usecase "UC-58\nSend cancellation/refund update" as UC58
  }
  package "Provider refund" #FFF7ED {
    usecase "UC-46\nSubmit/reconcile online refund" as UC46
  }
}

Event --> UC18
Event --> UC28
PayPal --> UC40
Event --> UC44
Event --> UC52
Event --> UC56
Event --> UC58
Event --> UC63
Time --> UC42
Time --> UC57
PayPal --> UC46

note bottom
"Booking event" and "Scheduled time" are triggers, not human users.
PayPal Sandbox is the external boundary; GoalZone remains the source of booking and refund state.
end note
@enduml
